language 0.1.0
module identity
  means
    Digital recognition of subjects, confirmation of their identity and the
    granting of authority to them within an information system.

entity principal : thing
  means
    principal: an entity to which authority may be granted and on whose behalf
    actions are performed.

entity identity : thing
  means
    identity: a set of claims by which a principal is recognised within a
    given system.

entity account : thing
  means
    account: a system-managed representation of an identity, having a
    lifecycle of its own.

entity credential : thing
  means
    credential: a secret or other verifiable object used to confirm an
    identity.

entity session : thing
  means
    session: a time-limited context of interaction bound to a confirmed
    identity.

entity role : thing
  means
    role: a named collection of authorities granted to a principal in a
    definite context.

entity permission : thing
  means
    permission: the right to perform a definite action upon a definite object
    or class of objects.
